SRC/biff -- biff, as built for OS-9/68000=========================================biff rewrites text in the style of B1FF, the Usenet caricature of anover-excited newcomer: upper case, `0' for `o', `C00L!!!', `WAREZ!1!!'.Written by Matt Welsh, 1992 (biff.x,v 1.1); from the `silly' collectionof joke filters posted to alt.sources in December 1992.  Its outputincludes profanity.ORIG holds biff.x as posted.biff.x is unchanged.  It is a lex program; lex.yy.c here was generatedin universe with this disk's flex 2.3 from biff.x.  biff.x carries itsown main; yywrap.c supplies the two-line yywrap that lex's library`-ll' used to provide.  rand() is linked from /dd/LIB/rand.r.  Theprogram never seeds it, so the random `I'/`1' and `S'/`5' choices comeout the same on every run, as they did on Unix.    echo "Please mend the computer program, thanks, you are cool" | biff    PLEEZ MEND THE C-64 WAREZ!1!!, THANX, U R C00L!!!